'''Shinobu Kocho''' is a [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event]]. She was added in [[Version 15.1 Update#Version 15.1.1 Update|Version 15.1.1]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 845
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Shinobu Kocho
|name2 = Shinobu Kocho CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Shinobu Kocho CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Shinobu Kocho is a high-pierce, [[Long Distance]] crowd-controller, tailored to punishing midrange and backline enemies such as [[I.M. Phace]] and [[Cala Maria]]. In practice, she's rather average all around with only a 50% chance to [[Weaken]] targets, somewhat made up for by two-part Multi-Hit that brings the average up to 75%.

She has an uncomfortably small inside range that allows melee pushers to infiltrate her blind spot relatively easily if her crowd-control fails to proc. This isn't helped by her actual target traits, which are jam-packed with hyper-aggressive and/or fast melees that are unrelenting. Her high pierce helps her hit a huge chunk of the battleground, and she is able to maintain a 100% uptime if you're lucky, but the impracticality of using her is to be noted.

While she can [[Critical Hit]], the 19% activation rate (per attack cycle) makes it a bonus for Metal stages while your actual [[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critters]] do most of the heavy lifting. However, when it does activate, it deals substantial damage, reaching 24,000 DPH at Lv.36, or just enough to instantly kill a 300% Super Metal Hippoe. As for [[Sage Slayer]], it's not very useful on her outside of [[Tarsiriel]] and [[Prof. Owlbrowley]], one of which is already shut down by [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Catcrates]] in large part.

